d I avoid the risk of losing more chips.  A check secures my win.\n\n**Answer: 0 (Check)**\n\n\n", 'output': "Evaluation: I have Two Pair, Eights and Fours, with a Ten kicker (Hand: 8-8-4-4-10). The opponent has shown extreme passivity by checking on every street (Pre-flop, Flop, Turn, River). This range suggests a weak hand, missed draws, or perhaps a weak pair. However, betting on the river is thin: worse hands (like Ace-high or small pairs) will likely fold, meaning I gain nothing extra, while better hands (any Ten, any Four, or an Eight with a kicker >10) will call or raise, causing me to lose chips. I also split with many weak Eights. Since I am currently in the lead in the overall match and the pot is small, minimizing variance and realizing my showdown value by checking is the optimal play.\n\nReason: I have a showdown-value hand (Two Pair) that beats bluffs and weak pairs but loses to any Ten or Four. The opponent's passive play suggests a weak hand. Betting likely only gets called by hands that beat me or split with me, while worse hands fold. Checking ensures I win the pot if I'm ahead without risking additional chips.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
